WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:02.330
(narrator)
Holding her own head aloft,

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:03.800
blood streaming into her mouth

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:05.630
and those of her
female followers,

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:08.800
feet planted on a
copulating couple,

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.690
Chinnamasta is an
audacious incarnation

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:12.559
of divine feminine energy.

00:00:12.559 --> 00:00:14.990
A Buddhist and Hindu
tantric goddess,

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:17.060
her name translates
from Sanskrit to

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:19.200
"She who is decapitated."

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.910
But while chopping
off your own head

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.680
seems like a pretty
decisive move,

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.730
Chinnamasta is, in fact, a
goddess of contradictions.

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:30.380
One who balances a fine line
between giving and receiving,

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:35.420
self-preservation and sacrifice,
reproduction and death.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:39.070
[light eerie music]

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:40.640
As a tantric goddess,

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.050
Chinnamasta rears
her distinctive head

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:44.740
across a range of
cultures and scriptures.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:48.090
Tantra, an intricate system
of beliefs and practices

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.570
that originated in India

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.480
in the middle of
the first millennium

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.489
is practiced by both
Hindus and Buddhists.

00:00:54.489 --> 00:00:57.239
Tantric rituals include the
use of mantras, meditation,

00:00:57.239 --> 00:00:59.100
coded language, and
deliberative gestures.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.550
They are intended to
channel enlightenment

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:03.330
through the physical body.

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.050
The Hindu tantric
tradition celebrates

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:08.540
the divine mother Devi or
Shakti, as a supreme deity

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:10.810
who comes in many
different manifestations,

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.800
from the demon-slayer Durga

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.780
to the golden Kamala,
Granter of Peace.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:18.659
The Dasa Mahavidyas,
or Great Wisdoms,

00:01:18.659 --> 00:01:21.100
are 10 interrelated
forms of Shakti

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.510
whose purpose is to
extend human awareness

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:25.950
beyond regular
levels of perception,

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:29.260
guiding their worshipers
towards fundamental truths.

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:31.600
Chinnamasta is the sixth
of these wisdom deities,

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:33.720
a fearsome figure
who can transcend

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:36.360
the limits of the mind.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:39.049
There are numerous origin
stories for Chinnamasta,

00:01:39.049 --> 00:01:41.940
but many involve a
combination of sex, hunger,

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:43.770
and radical sacrifice.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.310
In the Prana Toshini Tantra,

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:47.730
a collection of
Hindu tantric texts,

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:50.880
the gentle incarnation
of Shakti, Parvati,

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.890
was bathing outside
with two attendants.

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:57.340
Without warning, she became so
aroused that she turned black

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:59.240
and yet her two
hungry attendants

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:01.590
wouldn't stop
pestering her for food.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:02.869
They were so unrelenting

00:02:02.869 --> 00:02:05.689
that Parvati performed
a scandalous act.

00:02:05.689 --> 00:02:09.420
She sliced her head off with
her razor sharp fingernails,

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.250
assuming the form
of Chinnamasta,

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.439
the decapitated goddess.

00:02:13.439 --> 00:02:14.439
Blood gushed from her neck

00:02:14.439 --> 00:02:17.170
and poured into the
mouths of her attendants,

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:18.969
her severed head
catching the blood

00:02:18.969 --> 00:02:20.959
in her still living mouth.

00:02:20.959 --> 00:02:23.340
In another story from this
collection, Parvati and Shiva

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:25.340
were having an intimate moment,

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:27.489
but no sooner had
their passions abated,

00:02:27.489 --> 00:02:29.840
then here come those
two attendants again,

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:30.840
begging for food.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.859
Once again, Parvati severed
her head to nourish them

00:02:33.859 --> 00:02:36.400
and take the form
of Chinnamasta.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.550
In these versions of the story

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:40.849
hunger and sexual
desire are intertwined.

00:02:40.849 --> 00:02:42.739
Both appear
to sap human energy,

00:02:42.739 --> 00:02:45.079
but Chinnamasta
transforms these cravings

00:02:45.079 --> 00:02:46.959
into the source of power.

00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:48.069
Buddhist tantric texts

00:02:48.069 --> 00:02:50.849
named the decapitated
goddess as Chinnamunda,

00:02:50.849 --> 00:02:53.360
and there are subtle
differences between the two.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:55.430
But scholars generally
agree that Chinnamasta

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:58.340
and Chinnamunda are
the same goddess,

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:02.379
ones also known by 1,000 plus
names in tantric scripture.

00:03:02.379 --> 00:03:04.451
In Buddhist Tantrism,
Chinnamunda is a form

00:03:04.451 --> 00:03:07.180
of the Supreme
goddess, Vajrayogini,

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:10.760
a goddess who embodies
passion and love without ego.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:14.169
Buddhist texts do not explain
the origin of Chinnamunda,

00:03:14.169 --> 00:03:16.210
but there are several
manifestations of the goddess

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:18.109
who slice off their heads,

00:03:18.109 --> 00:03:20.379
including two sisters
and a princess

00:03:20.379 --> 00:03:22.359
who can decapitate
themselves at will

00:03:22.359 --> 00:03:25.260
to prove their divinity
to those who doubt them.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.839
As Chinnamunda, Vajrayogini
displays her supreme

00:03:27.839 --> 00:03:31.000
yogic ability and her
unattachment to ego.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.829
Whatever name she is going by,

00:03:32.829 --> 00:03:35.139
it's important to note that
the decapitated goddess

00:03:35.139 --> 00:03:39.969
is always able to place her
head back on her body at will,

00:03:39.969 --> 00:03:43.569
indicating her defiance of
death and powers of renewal.

00:03:43.569 --> 00:03:45.449
Across all texts, the
goddess is depicted

00:03:45.449 --> 00:03:49.139
with red or orange skin,
naked, save for her jewels,

00:03:49.139 --> 00:03:53.129
a garland of skulls and a
snake coiled around her waist.

00:03:53.129 --> 00:03:55.139
The skulls stand for
her ability to transcend

00:03:55.139 --> 00:03:58.159
the passage of time
and the fear of death.

00:03:58.159 --> 00:04:00.719
While the snake, as a
symbol of immortality,

00:04:00.719 --> 00:04:03.079
cements her everlasting life.

00:04:03.079 --> 00:04:05.900
Her lavish jewelry is
also rich with symbolism,

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:08.370
with her five mudras or
ornaments symbolizing

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:12.329
the five virtues of
giving, morality, patience,

00:04:12.329 --> 00:04:14.629
perseverance, and meditation.

00:04:14.629 --> 00:04:17.380
Chinnamasta's body itself
stands for a sixth virtue,

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:19.220
Prajna or insight.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:21.320
Her third eye reinforces
her possession

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:22.710
of a deeper form of knowledge,

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:25.600
as well as her balanced
perspective on past,

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.270
present, and future.

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:30.630
It's rare for Chinnamasta to
look directly at her devotees,

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:34.270
rather by looking unflinchingly
back at her severed body,

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:37.120
she directs her followers
to scrutinize themselves.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:39.900
It would take a lot more
than a bit of introspection

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:41.900
to make Chinnamasta flinch;

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:45.280
as suggested by her wielding
of a bloody sacrificial knife

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:47.450
and her warrior stance.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:50.070
With one foot advancing
in front of the other,

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:52.140
she stands poised to
defend her followers

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:55.600
and to destroy the
forces of ignorance.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:58.160
Chinnamasta certainly
cuts a shocking figure,

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:00.180
but while blood is more
commonly associated

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:01.610
with the demonic,

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:03.870
in this case it also
functions as a vital

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.040
and life-giving substance.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:09.580
By spilling her own blood and
feeding it to her followers,

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:11.700
Chinnamasta actively
converts bloodshed,

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:15.580
usually a symbol of draining
life, into a life force.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:17.070
But the question remains,

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:19.570
who benefits from
this life force?

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:22.340
Is Chinnamasta's self-beheading
an act of castration

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:24.150
that dilutes her powers?

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:25.430
By decapitating herself,

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:27.810
does she not make the
ultimate sacrifice

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:31.710
for her materially and
spiritually hungry attendants?

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:34.540
Decapitation is a common
trope in Indian mythology,

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:36.410
which is typically
inflicted as a punishment

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:38.960
or an act of self-annihilation.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:41.910
On the surface, a beheading
seems like a pretty fast way

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:43.520
to lose your agency.

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:45.670
But if we look a
little more closely,

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:48.280
characters who meet this
fate are often transformed

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.620
into something greater
than themselves.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:51.620
While losing your head

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:53.800
is undoubtedly
a violent occurrence,

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:55.680
it can also be about
severing the ego

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:58.110
and transcending
earthly circumstances

00:05:58.110 --> 00:06:00.160
for the sake of enlightenment.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:02.740
Similarly, Chinnamasta
appears to give herself up

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:04.380
to the needs of her attendants,

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:08.480
who pester her mercilessly for
food, even when she's busy.

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:10.631
In some texts, their
incessant demands cause her

00:06:10.631 --> 00:06:13.810
to turn her attention
away from her own arousal

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:16.050
and satisfaction, and
to redirect her energy

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:18.190
towards fulfilling their needs.

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.860
If we understand
giving and receiving

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:23.020
as fundamentally
opposed acts, then sure,

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:24.970
maybe it's giving up a
lot to chop off your head

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:28.030
and let your blood flow freely
just to please your friends,

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:31.380
but Chinnamasta is also gaining
something in the process.

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:34.140
By cutting off her head,
she liberates herself

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:35.990
from the perils of the mind,

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:39.940
like egotism, self-delusion
and toxic thought cycles.

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:42.080
This allows her to become
more present and powerful

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:44.700
in her body, which in
tantric teachings is seen

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:48.610
as the most important instrument
of spiritual enlightenment.

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:51.180
In this framing, nourishment,
sexual fulfillment,

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:54.020
and spiritual enlightenment
are not entities to be found

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:56.200
outside of one's self.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:59.170
Instead, Chinnamasta summons
the power to satiate herself.

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:01.620
Thus we can view
her shocking act

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:04.639
as one of self-preservation,
not sacrifice.

00:07:04.639 --> 00:07:06.570
At the same time,
this does not mean

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:08.860
that this is a selfish
spiritual quest.

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:11.100
Again, she's a goddess
who encourages us

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:14.290
to think beyond all
binaries, so buckle up.

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:17.360
Although Chinnamasta has
transcended all limitations,

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:19.670
her spiritual perfection
comes from her freedom

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:23.510
to help and nourish those who
are still on their journeys.

00:07:23.510 --> 00:07:25.730
Although her attendants
have their heads intact,

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:27.940
signaling their
relative inferiority,

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:30.310
the goddess's lack of ego
gives her the capacity

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:32.630
to aid all other beings.

00:07:32.630 --> 00:07:35.700
As she merges the role
of giver and receiver,

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:39.080
sacrificer and sacrificee,
subject and object,

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:42.060
she shatters the illusion
of duality itself

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:45.340
and reveals the interconnection
of all living things.

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:47.419
For this goddess,
even death and life

00:07:47.419 --> 00:07:49.160
are not really separate.

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:51.550
As the iconography of
her active fertile body

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:55.470
overlaid with deathly and
violent imagery suggests,

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:58.040
Chinnamasta experiences
both at once,

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:01.590
and therefore outstrips
earthly limitations.

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:03.410
Chinnamasta's highly
paradoxical position

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:07.180
is associated with both
destruction and reproduction.

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:08.710
In Buddhist tantric depictions,

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:10.860
she's usually planted on Kali,

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:13.630
a personification
of time and death,

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:14.919
indicating the
goddess's capacity

00:08:14.919 --> 00:08:17.090
to vanquish these forces.

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:18.700
In Hindu tantric depictions,

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:21.120
she has shown standing
upon Kama and Rati,

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:22.650
the gods of love and desire,

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:26.690
but is she trampling the famous
couple or protecting them?

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:29.310
In some cases, her position
above the couple may represent

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:30.860
her epic self-control;

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:34.199
just another way in which
Chinnamasta masters herself.

00:08:34.199 --> 00:08:35.930
It could also
indicate her mastery

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:38.279
of the cycle of life itself.

00:08:38.279 --> 00:08:40.430
With her ability to
perpetually obliterate

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:42.560
and re-enliven herself,

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:45.120
Chinnamasta becomes a powerful
symbol of reproduction

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.730
to rival the entwined couple.

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:49.259
Another reading might
focus on the imagery

00:08:49.259 --> 00:08:51.569
of the lotus flower
and inverted triangle

00:08:51.569 --> 00:08:54.129
that often appear
in these depictions.

00:08:54.129 --> 00:08:56.610
These signs associate
Chinnamasta with fertility,

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:59.610
abundant sexual energy,
and the divine feminine.

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:01.949
While the rest of the picture
keeps her bodily autonomy

00:09:01.949 --> 00:09:03.680
at the forefront.

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:05.610
Chinnamasta's Yantra
or geometric diagram

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:07.110
that acknowledges
her presence

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:09.370
and guides
meditation on the goddess,

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:11.140
also conjures the
divine feminine

00:09:11.140 --> 00:09:13.079
with its womb-like imagery.

00:09:13.079 --> 00:09:15.930
After drawing the symbol,
tantric scripture instructs

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:18.800
worshipers to offer
flowers, food, ornaments,

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:20.329
and more to the goddess.

00:09:20.329 --> 00:09:22.160
They also recite
suitable mantras

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:25.319
while meditating and
performing specific gestures.

00:09:25.319 --> 00:09:27.960
While these rituals and
their meanings survive,

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.110
Chinnamasta is not considered

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:31.470
a prominent tantric deity today.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.600
Shrines dedicated to
the goddess are rare,

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:36.220
but Chinnamasta surfaces
in many Hindu and Buddhist

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:38.010
paintings and practices.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.860
During the Hindu
festival of Kali Puja,

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:41.470
which celebrates Kali,

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:44.070
one neighborhood in the
Indian city of Cuttack

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:47.420
celebrates the goddess via
the veneration of Chinnamasta,

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:50.899
while many across India
celebrate Chinnamasta Jayanti,

00:09:50.899 --> 00:09:52.899
the goddess's designated day,

00:09:52.899 --> 00:09:54.269
by engaging in rituals

00:09:54.269 --> 00:09:57.160
to eliminate
negativity and longing.

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:58.899
As a figure who
nourishes herself

00:09:58.899 --> 00:10:00.990
while being consumed by others,

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:04.010
who fulfills herself as
she gives herself away

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:08.329
and who embraces destruction
even as she vanquishes death,

00:10:08.329 --> 00:10:11.100
Chinnamasta is a goddess
who dispels duality.

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:14.240
And although self-decapitation
is her signature act,

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:17.500
this doesn't mean that she
leaves her body behind.

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:19.499
Instead, Chinnamasta shows
us that we can nourish

00:10:19.499 --> 00:10:22.399
our physical bodies
and free our minds,

00:10:22.399 --> 00:10:24.910
and that these processes
are eternally intertwined.

00:10:26.009 --> 00:10:28.420
If you love the outdoors,
we think you'll really enjoy

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:30.500
the newest digital
series from PBS

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:33.029
called "America
Outdoors: Understory."

00:10:33.029 --> 00:10:34.629
Hosted by Baratunde Thurston,

00:10:34.629 --> 00:10:36.250
the show explores
our passionate,

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:37.639
yet complex relationship

00:10:37.639 --> 00:10:39.240
with the natural world.

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:40.670
Along the way, you
get to meet everyone

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:43.430
from surfing scientists
to fossil hunters.

00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:44.690
There's a link in
the description.

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:46.170
We hope you go check it out,

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:47.679
and then maybe go
get some fresh air.

00:10:47.679 --> 00:10:50.030
Accessibility provided by the
U.S. Department of Education.

